[
{
"start": 13.89,
"end": 16.89,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Notion replaces the dozen tools your team only half uses.",
"char_start": 14,
"char_end": 71,
"unit_id": "t0002.u01",
"sent_id": "t0002.s02"
},
{
"start": 16.89,
"end": 18.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Try notion.com today.",
"char_start": 72,
"char_end": 93,
"unit_id": "t0002.u01",
"sent_id": "t0002.s03"
},
{
"start": 18.0,
"end": 24.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Before we get started, Lena Hofmann was on the last episode and said that tire pressure is more important than suspension adjustments.",
"char_start": 94,
"char_end": 228,
"unit_id": "t0002.u01",
"sent_id": "t0002.s04"
},
{
"start": 24.0,
"end": 25.24,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Yes, exactly.",
"char_start": 244,
"char_end": 257,
"unit_id": "t0003.u01",
"sent_id": "t0003.s01"
},
{
"start": 25.24,
"end": 30.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And that connects to what we are discussing today.",
"char_start": 258,
"char_end": 308,
"unit_id": "t0003.u01",
"sent_id": "t0003.s02"
},
{
"start": 30.0,
"end": 36.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I'd like to point something out \u2013 Lena Hofmann mentioned the same dynamic a few episodes ago.",
"char_start": 323,
"char_end": 416,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s01"
},
{
"start": 36.0,
"end": 42.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I'd like to point something out \u2013 Stefan Brandt mentioned the same dynamic a few episodes ago.",
"char_start": 417,
"char_end": 511,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s02"
},
{
"start": 42.0,
"end": 43.77,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I want to delve deeper into that.",
"char_start": 512,
"char_end": 545,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s03"
},
{
"start": 43.77,
"end": 48.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What did you believe about it previously, and what have you revised since then?",
"char_start": 546,
"char_end": 625,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s04"
},
{
"start": 48.0,
"end": 51.05,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "In most cases, the mysterious creaking noises can be resolved by cleaning the contact surfaces and tightening them to the specified torque.",
"char_start": 641,
"char_end": 780,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s01"
},
{
"start": 51.05,
"end": 52.29,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this work with teams that use Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 781,
"char_end": 837,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s02"
},
{
"start": 52.29,
"end": 54.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The framing is important because it tells you what compromises you are making.",
"char_start": 838,
"char_end": 916,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s03"
},
{
"start": 54.0,
"end": 56.02,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "This is a useful framework.",
"char_start": 931,
"char_end": 958,
"unit_id": "t0006.u01",
"sent_id": "t0006.s01"
},
{
"start": 56.02,
"end": 60.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where do maintenance and the drive mechanism overlap?",
"char_start": 959,
"char_end": 1012,
"unit_id": "t0006.u01",
"sent_id": "t0006.s02"
},
{
"start": 60.0,
"end": 60.73,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's my perspective.",
"char_start": 1028,
"char_end": 1050,
"unit_id": "t0007.u01",
"sent_id": "t0007.s01"
},
{
"start": 60.73,
"end": 63.82,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "A bike should feel quiet and predictable, so that your attention remains focused on the trail.",
"char_start": 1051,
"char_end": 1145,
"unit_id": "t0007.u01",
"sent_id": "t0007.s02"
},
{
"start": 63.82,
"end": 66.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And the second-order effect is the part that most people overlook.",
"char_start": 1146,
"char_end": 1212,
"unit_id": "t0007.u01",
"sent_id": "t0007.s03"
},
{
"start": 66.0,
"end": 67.82,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I want to delve deeper into that.",
"char_start": 1227,
"char_end": 1260,
"unit_id": "t0008.u01",
"sent_id": "t0008.s01"
},
{
"start": 67.82,
"end": 72.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the structural perspective that most listeners don't have access to?",
"char_start": 1261,
"char_end": 1337,
"unit_id": "t0008.u01",
"sent_id": "t0008.s02"
},
{
"start": 72.0,
"end": 72.27,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Certainly.",
"char_start": 1353,
"char_end": 1363,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s01"
},
{
"start": 72.27,
"end": 74.49,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Chain wear is the best early indicator of when you need to replace your cassette.",
"char_start": 1364,
"char_end": 1445,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s02"
},
{
"start": 74.49,
"end": 75.89,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this with teams that use Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 1446,
"char_end": 1497,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s03"
},
{
"start": 75.89,
"end": 78.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The framing is important because it tells you what compromises you're making.",
"char_start": 1498,
"char_end": 1575,
"unit_id": "t0009.u01",
"sent_id": "t0009.s04"
},
{
"start": 78.0,
"end": 84.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Tell me more about it.",
"char_start": 1590,
"char_end": 1612,
"unit_id": "t0010.u01",
"sent_id": "t0010.s01"
},
{
"start": 84.0,
"end": 87.47,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Spoke & Wrench is one of the platforms where this becomes clearly visible.",
"char_start": 1628,
"char_end": 1702,
"unit_id": "t0011.u01",
"sent_id": "t0011.s01"
},
{
"start": 87.47,
"end": 90.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I have observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 1703,
"char_end": 1757,
"unit_id": "t0011.u01",
"sent_id": "t0011.s02"
},
{
"start": 90.0,
"end": 92.8,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Tell me how you made your decision.",
"char_start": 1772,
"char_end": 1807,
"unit_id": "t0012.u01",
"sent_id": "t0012.s01"
},
{
"start": 92.8,
"end": 96.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "How does RockShox fit into this picture?",
"char_start": 1808,
"char_end": 1848,
"unit_id": "t0012.u01",
"sent_id": "t0012.s02"
},
{
"start": 96.0,
"end": 96.19,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Sure.",
"char_start": 1864,
"char_end": 1869,
"unit_id": "t0013.u01",
"sent_id": "t0013.s01"
},
{
"start": 96.19,
"end": 99.33,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Service intervals for the suspension are a decision made by the risk management team.",
"char_start": 1870,
"char_end": 1955,
"unit_id": "t0013.u01",
"sent_id": "t0013.s02"
},
{
"start": 99.33,
"end": 102.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "If you ignore that, you'll have to rebuild it from scratch a year later.",
"char_start": 1956,
"char_end": 2028,
"unit_id": "t0013.u01",
"sent_id": "t0013.s03"
},
{
"start": 102.0,
"end": 102.37,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Guess what?",
"char_start": 2043,
"char_end": 2054,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s01"
},
{
"start": 102.37,
"end": 104.57,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "I'll just say it: Linear manages my entire engineering operations.",
"char_start": 2055,
"char_end": 2121,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s02"
},
{
"start": 104.57,
"end": 106.97,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Linear is the issue tracker built for speed \u2013 designed for keyboard use.",
"char_start": 2122,
"char_end": 2194,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s03"
},
{
"start": 106.97,
"end": 108.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Use the link in the show notes.",
"char_start": 2195,
"char_end": 2226,
"unit_id": "t0014.u01",
"sent_id": "t0014.s04"
},
{
"start": 126.0,
"end": 128.03,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "That's a helpful framework.",
"char_start": 2227,
"char_end": 2254,
"unit_id": "t0016.u01",
"sent_id": "t0016.s02"
},
{
"start": 128.03,
"end": 132.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where do maintenance and the drive mechanism overlap?",
"char_start": 2255,
"char_end": 2308,
"unit_id": "t0016.u01",
"sent_id": "t0016.s03"
},
{
"start": 132.0,
"end": 132.55,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's my understanding.",
"char_start": 2324,
"char_end": 2348,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s01"
},
{
"start": 132.55,
"end": 135.4,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Most mysterious creaking noises can be resolved by cleaning the contact surfaces and tightening them to the specified torque.",
"char_start": 2349,
"char_end": 2474,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s02"
},
{
"start": 135.4,
"end": 136.81,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this happen with teams that use Shimano components.",
"char_start": 2475,
"char_end": 2537,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s03"
},
{
"start": 136.81,
"end": 138.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 2538,
"char_end": 2590,
"unit_id": "t0017.u01",
"sent_id": "t0017.s04"
},
{
"start": 138.0,
"end": 139.36,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Give me a specific example.",
"char_start": 2605,
"char_end": 2632,
"unit_id": "t0018.u01",
"sent_id": "t0018.s01"
},
{
"start": 139.36,
"end": 144.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What did you used to believe about that, and what have you revised your views on since then?",
"char_start": 2633,
"char_end": 2725,
"unit_id": "t0018.u01",
"sent_id": "t0018.s02"
},
{
"start": 144.0,
"end": 147.69,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Yes, so \u2013 a bike should feel quiet and predictable, so that your attention remains focused on the trail.",
"char_start": 2741,
"char_end": 2845,
"unit_id": "t0019.u01",
"sent_id": "t0019.s01"
},
{
"start": 147.69,
"end": 150.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Once you understand that, the other decisions will become easier.",
"char_start": 2846,
"char_end": 2911,
"unit_id": "t0019.u01",
"sent_id": "t0019.s02"
},
{
"start": 150.0,
"end": 150.98,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Let's start there.",
"char_start": 2926,
"char_end": 2944,
"unit_id": "t0020.u01",
"sent_id": "t0020.s01"
},
{
"start": 150.98,
"end": 156.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What did you used to believe about that, and what have you revised your views on since then?",
"char_start": 2945,
"char_end": 3037,
"unit_id": "t0020.u01",
"sent_id": "t0020.s02"
},
{
"start": 156.0,
"end": 156.61,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's my perspective.",
"char_start": 3053,
"char_end": 3075,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s01"
},
{
"start": 156.61,
"end": 158.83,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Chain wear is the best early indicator of when you need to replace your cassette.",
"char_start": 3076,
"char_end": 3157,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s02"
},
{
"start": 158.83,
"end": 160.35,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this with teams that use Shimano components.",
"char_start": 3158,
"char_end": 3213,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s03"
},
{
"start": 160.35,
"end": 162.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Once you understand that, the other decisions become easier.",
"char_start": 3214,
"char_end": 3274,
"unit_id": "t0021.u01",
"sent_id": "t0021.s04"
},
{
"start": 162.0,
"end": 168.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "That fits.\nThat works.\nThat's perfect.\nThat's right.\nThat's a good fit.",
"char_start": 3289,
"char_end": 3360,
"unit_id": "t0022.u01",
"sent_id": "t0022.s01"
},
{
"start": 168.0,
"end": 174.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And when teams adopt the Spoke & Wrench process, the compromises become apparent. If you ignore these compromises, you'll end up having to rebuild everything from scratch a year later.",
"char_start": 3376,
"char_end": 3560,
"unit_id": "t0023.u01",
"sent_id": "t0023.s01"
},
{
"start": 174.0,
"end": 175.14,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Let's start there.",
"char_start": 3575,
"char_end": 3593,
"unit_id": "t0024.u01",
"sent_id": "t0024.s01"
},
{
"start": 175.14,
"end": 180.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the operational perspective that most listeners don't have access to?",
"char_start": 3594,
"char_end": 3671,
"unit_id": "t0024.u01",
"sent_id": "t0024.s02"
},
{
"start": 180.0,
"end": 180.74,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's how I see it.",
"char_start": 3687,
"char_end": 3707,
"unit_id": "t0025.u01",
"sent_id": "t0025.s01"
},
{
"start": 180.74,
"end": 184.01,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The service intervals for the suspension are a decision made by the risk management team.",
"char_start": 3708,
"char_end": 3797,
"unit_id": "t0025.u01",
"sent_id": "t0025.s02"
},
{
"start": 184.01,
"end": 186.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I have observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 3798,
"char_end": 3852,
"unit_id": "t0025.u01",
"sent_id": "t0025.s03"
},
{
"start": 186.0,
"end": 192.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Let's change the subject \u2013 I want to dedicate the final section to risk management.",
"char_start": 3867,
"char_end": 3950,
"unit_id": "t0026.u01",
"sent_id": "t0026.s01"
},
{
"start": 192.0,
"end": 198.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "That's where the conversation becomes interesting, because the compromises regarding risk management permeate everything we've discussed.",
"char_start": 3966,
"char_end": 4103,
"unit_id": "t0027.u01",
"sent_id": "t0027.s01"
},
{
"start": 198.0,
"end": 199.86,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Give me a specific example.",
"char_start": 4118,
"char_end": 4145,
"unit_id": "t0028.u01",
"sent_id": "t0028.s01"
},
{
"start": 199.86,
"end": 204.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the most underestimated part of the drive mechanism?",
"char_start": 4146,
"char_end": 4206,
"unit_id": "t0028.u01",
"sent_id": "t0028.s02"
},
{
"start": 204.0,
"end": 204.24,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Certainly.",
"char_start": 4222,
"char_end": 4232,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s01"
},
{
"start": 204.24,
"end": 207.31,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Most mysterious creaking noises can be resolved by cleaning the contact surfaces and tightening them to the specified torque.",
"char_start": 4233,
"char_end": 4358,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s02"
},
{
"start": 207.31,
"end": 208.73,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this happen with teams that use Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 4359,
"char_end": 4417,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s03"
},
{
"start": 208.73,
"end": 210.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 4418,
"char_end": 4470,
"unit_id": "t0029.u01",
"sent_id": "t0029.s04"
},
{
"start": 210.0,
"end": 211.6,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "This is a useful framework.",
"char_start": 4485,
"char_end": 4512,
"unit_id": "t0030.u01",
"sent_id": "t0030.s01"
},
{
"start": 211.6,
"end": 216.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the opposing perspective that most listeners are unable to access?",
"char_start": 4513,
"char_end": 4587,
"unit_id": "t0030.u01",
"sent_id": "t0030.s02"
},
{
"start": 216.0,
"end": 219.49,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "Ultimately, a bike should feel quiet and predictable, so that your attention remains focused on the trail.",
"char_start": 4603,
"char_end": 4709,
"unit_id": "t0031.u01",
"sent_id": "t0031.s01"
},
{
"start": 219.49,
"end": 222.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "The frame is important because it tells you what compromises you are making.",
"char_start": 4710,
"char_end": 4786,
"unit_id": "t0031.u01",
"sent_id": "t0031.s02"
},
{
"start": 222.0,
"end": 224.36,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What does the error scenario look like?",
"char_start": 4801,
"char_end": 4840,
"unit_id": "t0032.u01",
"sent_id": "t0032.s01"
},
{
"start": 224.36,
"end": 228.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the most underestimated part of the drive mechanism?",
"char_start": 4841,
"char_end": 4901,
"unit_id": "t0032.u01",
"sent_id": "t0032.s02"
},
{
"start": 228.0,
"end": 230.82,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "To be honest, chain wear is the best early indicator of when you need to replace your cassette.",
"char_start": 4917,
"char_end": 5012,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s01"
},
{
"start": 230.82,
"end": 232.46,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "We've seen this with teams that use Shimano components.",
"char_start": 5013,
"char_end": 5068,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s02"
},
{
"start": 232.46,
"end": 234.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 5069,
"char_end": 5121,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s03"
},
{
"start": 234.0,
"end": 240.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where does it break down?",
"char_start": 5136,
"char_end": 5161,
"unit_id": "t0034.u01",
"sent_id": "t0034.s01"
},
{
"start": 240.0,
"end": 246.0,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "And when teams adopt this process from Shimano, the compromise becomes apparent \u2013 I've observed this pattern in three different teams.",
"char_start": 5177,
"char_end": 5311,
"unit_id": "t0035.u01",
"sent_id": "t0035.s01"
},
{
"start": 246.0,
"end": 248.94,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "What is the heuristic that you always fall back on?",
"char_start": 5326,
"char_end": 5377,
"unit_id": "t0036.u01",
"sent_id": "t0036.s01"
},
{
"start": 248.94,
"end": 252.0,
"speaker_label": "Katrin Vogel",
"text": "Where do maintenance and the drive mechanism overlap?",
"char_start": 5378,
"char_end": 5431,
"unit_id": "t0036.u01",
"sent_id": "t0036.s02"
},
{
"start": 252.0,
"end": 255.6,
"speaker_label": "Jonas Richter",
"text": "To be honest, service intervals for the suspension are a decision made by the risk management team.",
"char_start": 5447,
